# What the project keeps out of version control.
#
# The rule changed when this became a multi-holding pipeline. It used to publish
# only the finished website; it now has to be able to rebuild that website from
# scratch, so the pipeline and the transcriptions travel with it. What stays out
# is bulk that can be re-derived, or that is not ours.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# COPYRIGHTED SOURCE - must never be committed or published.
# The Seidel (2018) biography is a research reference: facts and short cited
# quotations may appear in the edition, the book itself may not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Friedrich Ludwig, Fürst zu Hohenlohe-Ingelfingen*
*(2018, Seidel)*

# Archival masters, 1.7 GB. site/assets/scans/ carries the downscaled copies
# the site publishes, regenerated by make_scan_derivatives.py.
pages/

# Model output caches. Real money, and re-derivable by paying again, so they
# stay on this machine and are never published.
/cache/

# Generated review sheets and reports. Rebuilt on demand; the decisions they
# lead to are recorded in units/<slug>/rulings.yml and reference/, both tracked.
/review/

# Build output
site/_site/
site/.jekyll-cache/
site/.jekyll-metadata
site/vendor/
.bundle/

# Working files and one-offs left at the project root
/*.txt
/*.csv
/*.json
*.bak*
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# API credential
.anthropic_key

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
